---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
const evidence = '/api/v2/packages?monitor=security&search=observations&q=CVE-&include=security&detail=full&per_page=20';
const groupedURL = '/api/v2/packages?rva23_failed=AND&rva23_unresolvable=OR&Group=AND&Advisory=AND&DepMismatch=AND';
const batch = '/api/v2/packages:batchGet?names=bash&names=openssl&include=version&include=security';
---
<Base title="API">
  <article class="prose">
    <h1>API</h1>
    <p>Read-only snapshots. <a href="/openapi.json">OpenAPI: parameters and response schemas</a>.</p>

    <table class="data-table">
      <thead><tr><th scope="col">GET /api/v2</th><th scope="col">Returns</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td><a href="/api/v2/packages"><code>/packages</code></a></td>
          <td>Summaries + filter counts. <code>per_page</code>: default 100, max 200.
            <code>detail=full</code> adds evidence and requires <code>per_page≤20</code>.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><a href="/api/v2/packages/bash"><code>/packages/{'{name}'}</code></a></td>
          <td>Full package observations.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>/packages:batchGet</code></td>
          <td>Full observations for 1–20 unique packages. Repeat <code>names</code> to specify request order.
            Any missing name fails the batch.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><a href="/api/v2/tracks/meson"><code>/tracks/{'{id}'}</code></a></td><td>Saved version-track observation.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><a href="/api/v2/targets"><code>/targets</code></a></td><td>OBS target identities.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><a href="/api/v2/status"><code>/status</code></a></td><td>Collection freshness, coverage and errors.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><a href="/api/v2/export"><code>/export</code></a></td><td>Complete, unpaginated snapshot, schema 2.</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>

    <h2>Queries</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><code>monitor</code> focuses filtering. Repeated <code>include</code> selects returned monitors
        (default: all). IDs come from the list response's <code>monitors</code>.</li>
      <li><code>q</code> searches names. <code>search=observations</code> adds fact values,
        restricted by <code>monitor</code> when set. Matching uses case-insensitive substrings.</li>
      <li>Ordinary search: <code>?Outdated&amp;Yanked</code>. Conditions intersect.
        States of the same build target and BuildSystems form unions:
        <code>?rva23_failed+rva23_succeeded&amp;Yanked</code>,
        <code>?buildsystem_cmake+buildsystem_pyproject</code>.</li>
      <li>Advanced Search: <code>?Outdated=AND&amp;Advisory=OR&amp;EOL=NOT</code>.
        Operations run left to right from ALL. <code>Group=AND|OR|NOT</code>
        seals the preceding ungrouped conditions. Each group starts from ALL and cannot nest.
        <code>advanced=1</code> opens the editor without conditions. Do not mix bare flags and operators.</li>
      <li>Ordinary counts show intersections. Alternatives within a selected build target or BuildSystem count additions under the other conditions.
        Advanced Search uses <code>next_logic=and|or|not</code> (default: and): AND counts matches, OR counts additions, NOT counts removals.
        The operator affects counts, not current results. Each package counts once within the search and focused view.
        Check counts target coverage.</li>
    </ul>
    <p><a href={groupedURL}>Build alternatives intersected with two alerts</a>:</p>
    <pre><code>{groupedURL}</code></pre>
    <p>Use <code>dimension/value</code> for other predicates, such as
      <code>check:security/error</code>. The response includes the normalized query and
      <code>query_node_limit</code>: conditions plus explicit or implicit union groups.
      Raw repeated conditions count before deduplication. Invalid or oversized queries return 422.</p>
    <p>Find advisory evidence:</p>
    <pre><code><a href={evidence}>{evidence}</a></code></pre>
    <p>Fetch known packages:</p>
    <pre><code><a href={batch}>{batch}</a></code></pre>

    <p><code>404</code> missing resource · <code>422</code> invalid package query · <code>503</code> no snapshot.<br />
      Preserve <code>check</code> and <code>stale</code>. Null means unknown.
      One snapshot per response, not across pages.</p>
    <p><code>check.failures</code> identifies failed subchecks, including partial results.
      <code>check_groups</code> counts the <code>uncovered</code> and <code>failed</code> filters.
      <code>check_statuses</code> retains the individual states.</p>
    <p>Website display documents: <a href="/api/ui/packages">/api/ui/packages</a>,
      <a href="/api/ui/packages/bash">/api/ui/packages/{'{name}'}</a>.</p>
  </article>
</Base>
<style>
  pre { white-space: pre-wrap; }
</style>
